#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "00b886e2-e15e-5b9e-a371-7c8e659febb1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12947" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f6fb8d85c6e0921d49f16b410a3c3d7c549caabb166b0e65bb4c1982844310c3.png)\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is a square matrix\n\n- $A \\cdot A^T = I$\n\n- $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA \\cdot A^T = A^T\\cdot A = I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n![](images/3e/3e419059afe53ef90b1c086f75c29513e7f6cc269ac4ecbf16e0db919222b3f5.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A\\cdot A^T = I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "b87bd2f0-67da-5b9d-9e21-831afa44eec8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12948" :question/problem "![](images/08/08c339defb7800dfbafef33db26281a6eb44740a61ff9d47bae8e9adc6af5f75.png)\n\nFind $|\\textrm{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(-2\\sqrt{3})\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}-2\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-18-2| \\\\  & =|-20| \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9d50c0e3-386e-57db-b509-bed0d933e6ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-12949" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix ![](images/0f/0fdcc6a3e329666b00a45c05292d85ab2df6366ff38d5506233b6c15064d2149.png)" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nTherefore, since $D$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{-1} & ={D}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "848f3901-12b3-5a37-bb03-08743e7058c8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12950" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\n- $2Q$ is orthogonal\n\n- $P^{-1}Q$ is orthogonal\n\n- $PQ^T$ is orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ Q^T = Q^T Q = I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have $Q^{-1} = Q^T.$\n\n- $(AB)^T = B^TA^T$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the product $2Q \\cdot (2Q)^T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2Q\\cdot (2Q)^{T} & =2Q\\cdot 2{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =4Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =4I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the product $(P^{-1}Q)\\cdot (P^{-1}Q)^T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({P}^{-1}Q)\\cdot ({P}^{-1}Q)^{T} & =({P}^{T}Q)\\cdot ({P}^{T}Q)^{T} \\\\  & ={P}^{T}Q\\cdot {Q}^{T}({P}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={P}^{T}(Q{Q}^{T})P \\\\  & ={P}^{T}(I)P \\\\  & ={P}^{T}P \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Computing the product $(PQ^T)\\cdot(PQ^T)^T ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P{Q}^{T})\\cdot (P{Q}^{T})^{T} & =P{Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T}{P}^{T} \\\\  & =P{Q}^{T}Q{P}^{T} \\\\  & =P({Q}^{T}Q){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(I){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e43a7a4-61dd-55ec-ac22-f5f69dc1275a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8}{17} & \\frac{15}{17} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365033} {:answer/id #uuid "fa352170-de9d-577d-8a45-161b02256251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{17} & \\frac{15}{17} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365034} {:answer/id #uuid "70c31298-70c6-5e44-939c-7298d4a5a16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8}{17} & \\frac{15}{17} \\\\ \\frac{15}{17} & -\\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365035} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5ee8fa-6107-51dc-ac45-c48f635f9e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ is not invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365036} {:answer/id #uuid "4e124c1e-5d1b-539c-af6f-7ee8d04d6b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{17} & -\\frac{15}{17} \\\\ \\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e124c1e-5d1b-539c-af6f-7ee8d04d6b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{17} & -\\frac{15}{17} \\\\ \\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365037} :answer-field/id #uuid "be68f4d8-23a0-5fb9-8946-0f0a127eb8fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "799244d5-bb2f-52af-ab58-533edeceb08d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140562" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{17} & \\frac{15}{17} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nTherefore, since $D$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{-1} & ={D}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{17} & -\\frac{15}{17} \\\\ \\frac{15}{17} & \\frac{8}{17}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166cacd8-7020-5f1c-86a5-0227fea99376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269457} {:answer/id #uuid "21c788c6-1356-57a2-82a0-5f5207d35468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269559} {:answer/id #uuid "24c0b08e-bf14-5222-ab2b-25191a1a367a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269592} {:answer/id #uuid "a9468d13-9fb6-50d4-9618-5f4c85674da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270778} {:answer/id #uuid "dd314a8d-8509-5487-9dae-61cddef0e332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "166cacd8-7020-5f1c-86a5-0227fea99376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269457} :answer-field/id #uuid "8681c451-1220-56a4-bf52-1ccbfa0f5a57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37be5226-f355-5da6-9310-01c6af117505" :question/math-academy-id "q-140563" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} & \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98311a5d-c789-50b1-998c-82789cf3e15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464132} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1caad2-1552-53b2-ad65-0faf937f9cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1caad2-1552-53b2-ad65-0faf937f9cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464133} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d3e7a6-f070-518f-bca6-72c0a2e523f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2950a552-7b64-54f3-9df5-37fbc1daf708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464134} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc0bcf-2d74-5b42-80b8-a9462aac80d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2950a552-7b64-54f3-9df5-37fbc1daf708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464134} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e24475-4728-5731-901b-4204e0ce6cef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427e5f77-75e3-5ea5-8f93-8f5a66733617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464136} {:answer/id #uuid "01222f75-c4bd-542d-8467-b02dd4c8ea9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427e5f77-75e3-5ea5-8f93-8f5a66733617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464136} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74724c4-d89e-52f6-b857-07eecbd822cb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3d61daa-c943-5ecf-a98c-7f9bcd210491" :question/math-academy-id "q-140565" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrix $Q$ and the $n\\times n$ matrix $P?$\n- **I.** If $\\lambda $ is a real eigenvalue of $Q,$ then $\\lambda =\\pm 1$\n- **II.** If the determinant of $P$ is either $1$ or $-1,$ then $P$ is orthogonal\n- **III.** $Q-I$ is singular\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $\\lambda $ is an eigenvalue of an orthogonal matrix $Q$ then $\\lambda =\\pm 1$\n\n- Statement II is false. Every orthogonal matrix has the determinant equal to $\\pm 1$, but not every matrix with the determinant equal to $\\pm 1$ is orthogonal. As a counterexample, consider the following matrix:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe determinant of $P$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P)=2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n however, $P$ is not orthogonal since, for example, the first column is not normalized.\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the following orthogonal matrix:\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\nQ-I=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand $Q-I$ is not singular since, for example, it doesn't have proportional rows or columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b83cbcb7-0b07-5ebc-aa53-89e2be0b52df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450114} {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115} :answer-field/id #uuid "f129ca4a-c8e7-580b-91d4-1a0d29e6e4ed" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} {:answer/id #uuid "72a3e0ac-77bc-591c-8e67-8888858b7e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} :answer-field/id #uuid "e642ba26-55cc-5b02-a022-90bbe00ce622" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} {:answer/id #uuid "990655aa-5186-5262-8a17-20c96c8aacfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d44e42c-bf19-521c-a0c4-c2026051681e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ef1bd48-9355-501c-9dc0-0c7250b226e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-177663" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8747a7f2-4782-567d-a33d-1976b4319f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131492} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdd2de1-d1b1-59a8-9996-032691e9c297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131493} {:answer/id #uuid "1f8ca333-9069-5e36-9544-dcd776fef133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131494} {:answer/id #uuid "2b874229-0fc4-54ae-9694-c54b40eaf52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131495} {:answer/id #uuid "491f8950-37c1-5863-8464-15a98cdf15c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131496}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c1b3bc70-0e0f-5fed-8f78-181f20b95555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131491}] :question/id #uuid "ab7c31a0-8694-52ae-9c85-3e23bf4389e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39867" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax = b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/r